# Single Source of Truth

Every piece of information lives in exactly one place. Outdated docs are worse than no docs.

## Before creating any new doc, file, or Confluence page

Ask: **does a page/file already covering this topic exist?**

- If yes → **update it**. Do not create a new page alongside it.
- If no → create one, and note where it lives so future updates go there.

## Confluence

- Architecture → `CTO Architecture Diagram` (page ID 5931010)
- Tech Stack → `Tech Stack` (page ID 5177364)
- Security → pages under `AuraFlux / Security`
- Product audit → pages under `AuraFlux / Product`
- Do NOT create standalone pages for topics already covered by the above

## Codebase

- Stale comments must be removed or updated when the code they describe changes
- Stale `.md` files in `docs/` must be updated or deleted — not added to
- `STATUS.md` is updated on every commit (enforced by pre-commit hook)
- `README.md` and `CONTRIBUTING.md` are updated when public-facing behaviour changes

## Rule

If you catch yourself creating a new doc instead of updating an existing one, stop.
Find the existing doc and add a section to it.
